1. centralise it for easy to maintenance is a good common practise. otherwise, when we add/modify a section or item, we have to go through many files. multi language files solution will quickly lead to unsync and errors in different language environment. 

2. in one json, we can take the advantages of co-pilot or any AI to easy fill in other language based on initial like this. 
    "task_with_context": {
      "el": "{task}
Αυτό είναι το πλαίσιο με το οποίο εργάζεστε:
{context}",
      "en": "{task}
This is the context you're working with:
{context}",
      "cn": "{task}
这是您正在使用的上下文：
{context}",
      "fr": "{task}
Voici le contexte avec lequel vous travaillez:
{context}",
      "jp": "{task}
これがあなたが働いているコンテキストです：
{context}",
      "kr": "{task}
이것은 당신이 일하고있는 문맥입니다 :
{context}",
      "ru": "{task}
Это контекст, с которым вы работаете:
{context}",
      "de": "{task}
Dies ist der Kontext, mit dem Sie arbeiten:
{context}",
    }

3. if your concern is loading i18n on every script will be too costly because of the file size. we can work out a singleton class to handle it at the app initial stage.

